{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794246108,"nonce":"t2NrMxtkkeT+h4B8FQtAa7uUIeQ=","title":"jno.rcwa cannot sample a region-attached permittivity","message":"A permittivity given per region (.attach(eps=...), i.e. domain.eps = sum RegionMask(r) * eps_r) fails in RCWA's grid sampler: 'ValueError: Cannot evaluate: \u003cclass jno.trace.RegionMask\u003e'. RegionMask is resolved per cell inside jno.fem's kernels only, so the same constraint list could not be handed to both solvers.\n\nFix: region_membership_at(domain, region, X) gives point membership by the geometric rule _cell_region_mask uses at centroids (geometry part, tag predicate, shape.regions with priority subtraction). by_region masks remember their domain; RCWA puts the sample points' membership in the evaluation context; TraceEvaluator reads it there. A mesh-file volume region has no point membership and raises by name.\n\nTest: tests/test_rcwa_vector.py::test_a_region_attached_permittivity_matches_the_same_coordinate_function (region eps vs the same eps as a coordinate function).","files":null}]}